---
title: Smash burgers
servings: 2
tags: [american, beef, weeknight, quick]
cuisine: american
source: Smashed Burgers by America's Test Kitchen, https://wskg.org/americas-test-kitchen-smashed-burgers-ep-2116/
---

== Sauce ==

Stir together the @mayonnaise{2%tbsp}, @shallot{1%tbsp}(minced),
@dill pickles{1 1/2%tsp}(finely chopped) plus 1/2 tsp of their brine,
@ketchup{1 1/2%tsp}, @sugar{1/8%tsp} and @black pepper{1/8%tsp}.

== Burgers ==

Spread a tablespoon of sauce on the cut side of each top half of the
@hamburger buns{2}(toasted if you like).

Divide the @ground beef{8%oz}(80% lean) into four 2 oz pieces and shape them
into loose balls without packing them.

Rub the @vegetable oil{1/4%tsp} over the base of a 12-inch #cast-iron skillet{}
and heat over medium-low ~{5%minutes}. Wrap the base and sides of a
#small saucepan{} in foil to use as a press.

Turn the heat to high. When the pan smokes, set two balls in it 3 inches apart
and press each flat to 4 to 4 1/2 inches across.

Season with half the @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and some pepper. Cook ~{2%minutes},
until the tops are mostly no longer pink.

Loosen, flip, cook ~{15%seconds}, and slide the pan off the heat. Put one
patty on each bun bottom and top with a slice of @American cheese{2%slices}.

Scrape and wipe the pan, put it back on the heat, and cook the other two the
same way. Stack them on the cheese.

Add @butter lettuce{}(Bibb leaves) and @tomato{}(thinly sliced), close the buns, and
serve at once.
